nner", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Adverbs of Frequency - How Often", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\"> Adverbs of frequency</span> (<span class=\"italic\"> always, usually, never</span>, etc.) say how often something happens.  ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "This coffee shop is <span class=\"strong\">always</span>  busy.\t", "type": "example"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":\"05\",\"columns\":\"02\",\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\"> Adverbs</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">How often? </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"always\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"100%\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"usually\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"60%\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"rarely\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"10%\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"never\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"0%\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "You usually put adverbs of frequency before the verb. <br />", "type": "text"}, {"content": " I <span class=\"strong\">usually </span> go for a walk in the neighborhood. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I <span class=\"strong\">always </span> eat dinner in the kitchen.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "The adverb can <span class=\"italic\">sometimes</span>  be in different positions in the sentence. For example, you put the adverb of frequency after the verb <span class=\"strong\">to be</span>. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I <span class=\"strong\">always</span> go to yoga class on Wednesdays.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Susan <span class=\"strong\"> rarely</span> eats breakfast. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Robert <span class=\"strong\">never</span> drinks tea.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "always", "type": "name"}, {"content": "at all times", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adverb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I always have coffee in the morning.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn1le04ob08aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use when you talk about daily activities.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "never", "type": "name"}, {"content": "not ever; at no time", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adverb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I never take the bus to school.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn1le04ob08aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "usually", "type": "name"}, {"content": "regularly; normally", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adverb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I usually have a sandwich for lunch.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn1le04ob08aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "sometimes", "type": "name"}, {"content": "now and then; not all the time", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adverb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I sometimes go to the market when I need bread.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn1le04ob08aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "take a break", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to have a little time away from my work", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I take a break at ten o'clock.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn1le04ob08aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_wor